the sheriff is about to take on crypto's  wild west  [Music]  imagine being able to print dollars on  u.s soil and doing so without being  regulated  stablecoins are part of the backbone of  the cryptocurrency universe  together accounting for 120 billion  dollars they're used as a place to park  your money with bitcoin ether and other  cryptos are volatile some investors use  them as saving accounts or for posting  margin for trading digital assets  what they all have in common is that  they try to hold an unchanging value in  reference to some other real world  currency like the dollar or euro  and until now there's been very little  oversight the biggest  tether said until 2019 that for every  one of its units outstanding it held a  dollar in reserve  then in february of that year it said it  may also be backed by cash equivalents  and other assets  that makes it like a money market fund  except that it doesn't have to publish  which assets it owns as regulated funds  do the problem is that this can create a  feedback loop into the real economy  if there's a run on tether it may have  to sell its money market instruments  which may create a liquidity crunch in  other debt assets  and that could create a systemic risk  for financial markets  this is why the u.s securities and  exchange commission is paying attention  chair gary gensler has taken a hard line  on cryptocurrencies in general  he's part of the president's working  group along with jerome powell and janet  yellen but new york attorney general  leticia james has gone further  in february she required tether to end  all trading activity with new yorkers  tethers claims that its virtual currency  was fully backed by u.s dollars at all  times was a lie she said  so right now the sheriffs are looking  for a fight and the wild west is about  to be tamed  i'm eddie van der waalt this is  decrypted for more content like this  follow us on your favorite platforms  you
 

